The Orb OS: lineage and attribution
===================================

This file exists because the LICENSE cannot hold it. GitHub identifies a
licence by matching the file against the exact text of a known one, and prose
inserted into the middle of MIT's wording defeats that match. The repository
then reads as "NOASSERTION" rather than "MIT", which is the single word a
developer looks for before deciding whether they are allowed to use anything
here. So the licence is now verbatim MIT, and the history it used to carry
lives here instead, still travelling with the software exactly as before.

Everything below about who did what is taken from the repository's own git
history and commit messages. `git shortlog -sne` and `git log` are the
authority; this is a readable summary of them.

Origin
------

The Orb OS began as a fork of Quique Tortosa's Capsule Radar, and was called
Capsule Radar itself until August 2026. The original copyright is retained in
LICENSE, as MIT requires.

What is Zion Brock's later work
-------------------------------

Substantial later work is Zion Brock's: the clock, menu, settings, news and
startup screens, the SD-card theme engine, the Orb Studio serial and WiFi
protocols, and the flash art pipeline.

The Orb Studio protocols and their release scripts were removed from this
fork on 2026-09-20 ("Docs: this fork no longer uses Orb Studio"), so they are
part of the history rather than of the current tree. The theme format that
replaced the Studio's is described under Geoff Ford's work below.

Contributions merged from other people
--------------------------------------

Four pull requests from other people are in the history, credited in their
commit messages, and their work is still in the firmware:

  - Display: arbitrary per-degree rotation (PR #8), by @diliadis
  - Weather suite: 3-day forecast, precipitation radar and satellite clouds
    (PR #9), by @ChrispyBacon-dev
  - Feed: reliable JSON stream, and retaining contacts through brief empty
    responses (PR #5), by @liminghuang
  - Build: quoting the include path in platformio.ini (PR #6), by @vlucent

What is Geoff Ford's work
-------------------------

From 2026-09-19, Geoff Ford's commits begin. The main areas are:

  - the source tree restructure into app, core, platform and theme;
  - the `theme.yaml` format and its builder (tools/build_theme.py), which
    replaced the Studio's theme export, and the Fallout, Portal and Vault-Tec
    themes;
  - colour roles (a theme is four colours and the firmware derives the rest),
    the built-in default look, and named typeface faces shared between slots;
  - the drawn clock face, and the removal of the compiled skins, artwork and
    bitmap fonts;
  - touch swipes, and Weather as three knob-selected screens;
  - the shared PNG decoder, the SD-card guard, the settings store, and the
    host test suite;
  - the screenshot tools (tools/themeshots.sh, tools/shot_diff.py);
  - the single wheel that draws both the app picker and Settings.

AI assistance
-------------

Several hundred commits, by all three of the main authors above, carry a
